---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout
  title="Home"
  description="Plastic Circle West Africa establishes locally managed circular-economy systems in Sierra Leone and The Gambia that collect, sort and transform plastic waste into marketable products, creating jobs, skills and measurable environmental impact."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal">Ayara Foundation Switzerland</p>
      <h1 class="reveal">Plastic Circle West Africa</h1>
      <p class="lede reveal">
        Circular plastic recovery, local manufacturing and green jobs in Sierra Leone
        and The Gambia. We turn plastic waste into marketable products, while
        building local skills, income and measurable environmental impact.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta reveal">
        <a class="pill-btn" href="#platforms">See the Country Platforms</a>
        <a class="pill-btn outline on-dark" href={`${base}contact`}>Partner With Us</a>
      </div>

      <div class="stat-bar">
        <div class="stat">
          <p class="stat-label">Sierra Leone</p>
          <p class="stat-value">~130,000 t</p>
          <p class="stat-note">plastic waste per year &middot; under 10% currently recycled</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <p class="stat-label">The Gambia</p>
          <p class="stat-value">~23,000 t</p>
          <p class="stat-note">plastic waste per year &middot; ~84% inadequately managed</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <p class="stat-label">Programme scale</p>
          <p class="stat-value">2 country platforms</p>
          <p class="stat-note">36-month implementation &middot; local jobs, trained collectors and recovered plastic across both sites</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Why this matters</p>
        <h2>Plastic as a local resource, not a local burden</h2>
        <p>
          Plastic pollution in Sierra Leone and The Gambia is an environmental,
          infrastructure and livelihoods challenge at once. Rather than treating
          plastic purely as waste, Plastic Circle West Africa connects waste
          management with manufacturing, employment and market development,
          so that recovered material becomes income, jobs and cleaner
          communities.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">The model</p>
        <h2>From waste leakage to local value creation</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid reveal">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>1. Recover</h3>
          <p>
            Neighbourhood and institutional collection, local collectors,
            labelled drop-off points and public campaigns create a reliable
            plastic feedstock.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>2. Prepare</h3>
          <p>
            Plastic is sorted by type, colour and quality, then cleaned and
            prepared for production under clear quality and safety procedures.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>3. Make</h3>
          <p>
            Locally operated machinery shreds, presses and forms recovered
            plastic into furniture, outdoor products, interior elements,
            surfaces, household goods and customised products.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>4. Sell &amp; Reinvest</h3>
          <p>
            Product sales and services create local revenue, with surpluses
            reinvested into operations, jobs, maintenance and gradual
            expansion.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section panel wine" id="platforms" style="margin: 0 clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2.5rem); width:auto; padding: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem) clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--blush);">Country platforms</p>
      <h2>One model, two local platforms</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Plastic Loop</strong> (The Gambia) and <strong>DecoPlastic</strong>
        (Sierra Leone) apply the same core recovery-to-manufacturing model under
        the Plastic Circle West Africa umbrella, each adapted to local waste
        streams, market demand, institutions and community structures, and each
        led by an established local implementation partner.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid cols-2 reveal">
      <a class="platform-card" href={`${base}sierra-leone`} style="color:inherit;">
        <div class="platform-head">
          <span class="country">Sierra Leone</span>
          <h3 style="margin:0;">DecoPlastic</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="platform-body">
          <p>
            A locally rooted plastic collection, sorting and manufacturing
            system for Sierra Leone, led by Sierra Leone Engineering Solutions.
          </p>
          <span class="text-link">Explore Sierra Leone &rarr;</span>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a class="platform-card" href={`${base}gambia`} style="color:inherit;">
        <div class="platform-head">
          <span class="country">The Gambia</span>
          <h3 style="margin:0;">Plastic Loop</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="platform-body">
          <p>
            A circular plastic recovery and manufacturing system for the
            Greater Banjul Area, led by Hustle for Humanity Gambia.
          </p>
          <span class="text-link">Explore The Gambia &rarr;</span>
        </div>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Impact at a glance</p>
        <h2>Six ways this programme creates value</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid reveal">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Cleaner waters &amp; biodiversity</h3>
          <p>Plastic kept out of rivers, mangroves and coastal waters, protecting aquatic and marine life.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Circular economy, less waste</h3>
          <p>Plastic recovered, reused and made into products, cutting demand for virgin material.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Decent work &amp; local value</h3>
          <p>Local green jobs and income, with collectors fairly integrated and better earnings.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Women &amp; youth included</h3>
          <p>Clear targets for women's participation and a strong focus on young people.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Healthier communities</h3>
          <p>Cleaner neighbourhoods, better waste management and lower public-health risks.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Climate action</h3>
          <p>Less open burning of plastic and protection of carbon-storing mangroves.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Focus</p>
        <h2>Four dimensions of impact</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid cols-2 reveal">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Environmental</h3>
          <p>
            Plastic diverted from drains, rivers, mangroves and coasts and
            converted into productive use, with avoided emissions from
            reduced open burning.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Social</h3>
          <p>
            Inclusive jobs, training and safer, more structured participation
            for collectors, with deliberate targets for women and young
            people.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Economic</h3>
          <p>
            A local value chain from waste to product, growing revenue,
            buyers and services, and rising local cost recovery over time.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Operational</h3>
          <p>
            Resilient production through hybrid energy, quality control and
            durable local partnerships and sourcing agreements.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Partnership &amp; delivery</p>
        <h2>Who delivers the programme</h2>
        <p>
          Plastic Circle West Africa is delivered through a Swiss-led
          partnership with established local implementation organisations
          and a shared technology partner.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid reveal">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Ayara Foundation Switzerland</h3>
          <p>
            Programme lead: strategy, technical direction, governance,
            fundraising and international partnerships, in close
            collaboration with the local lead partners.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>ECOLLABO8</h3>
          <p>
            Technology partner: recycling machinery, technical onboarding,
            production know-how and training for local teams.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Aquitas (Switzerland)</h3>
          <p>
            MEAL and evidence partner: baseline design, indicators, data
            quality, outcome monitoring, learning and evaluation, with no
            implementation role.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Hustle for Humanity Gambia</h3>
          <p>
            Local implementation lead for Plastic Loop, The Gambia:
            operational coordination, community engagement and stakeholder
            mobilisation. <a class="text-link" href={`${base}gambia`}>More &rarr;</a>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Sierra Leone Engineering Solutions</h3>
          <p>
            Local implementation lead for DecoPlastic, Sierra Leone:
            operational coordination, local stakeholder engagement and
            sourcing relationships. <a class="text-link" href={`${base}sierra-leone`}>More &rarr;</a>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Swiss technical partner (ETH domain)</h3>
          <p>
            Recycling and production quality support, process design and
            applied know-how, complementing ECOLLABO8's machinery and
            training.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="positions" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Open positions</p>
        <h2>Join a local team</h2>
        <p>
          As each country platform moves from setup into operations, Plastic
          Circle West Africa and its local implementation partners are
          building local teams in collection, production, design, finance
          and community engagement. Roles below are recruited in
          anticipation of donor approval; more positions will be added as
          Sierra Leone and The Gambia scale up.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="job-list reveal">
        <div class="job-item">
          <div class="job-main">
            <h3>Senior Finance and Administrative Officer</h3>
            <p>
              Plastic Loop Gambia &middot; Greater Banjul Area &middot;
              full-time, 12-month contract, renewable
            </p>
            <p>
              Oversees financial management and administrative operations for
              the project: budgeting, financial reporting, donor compliance,
              procurement and general office administration, reporting to the
              Local Project Lead.
            </p>
            <div class="job-tags">
              <span class="tag">Hustle for Humanity Gambia</span>
              <span class="tag">Finance &amp; Admin</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="job-apply">
            <a class="text-link" href="mailto:plasticloopgambia@gmail.com?subject=Senior%20Finance%20and%20Administrative%20Officer">Apply by email &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="job-item">
          <div class="job-main">
            <h3>Workshop Fabrication Lead</h3>
            <p>
              Plastic Loop Gambia &middot; Greater Banjul Area &middot;
              full-time, 12-month contract, renewable
            </p>
            <p>
              Coordinates and supervises workshop fabrication activities,
              ensuring safe, efficient, high-quality production in line with
              approved drawings, specifications and quality standards.
            </p>
            <div class="job-tags">
              <span class="tag">Hustle for Humanity Gambia</span>
              <span class="tag">Production</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="job-apply">
            <a class="pill-btn outline" href={`${base}documents/plastic-loop-gambia-workshop-fabrication-lead.pdf`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Download Job PDF</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="more-note reveal">More roles will be posted here as recruitment opens for DecoPlastic in Sierra Leone and as Plastic Loop Gambia scales up.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section panel wine" style="margin: 0 clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2.5rem) clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem); width:auto; padding: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem) clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); text-align:center;">
    <h2>Partner with Plastic Circle West Africa</h2>
    <p style="max-width:560px; margin: 0 auto 1.5em;">
      Ayara Foundation Switzerland is seeking grant, co-funding and strategic
      partners for one or both country platforms, including local
      implementation, technical and distribution partnerships.
    </p>
    <a class="pill-btn outline on-dark" href={`${base}contact`}>Get in Touch</a>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero-cta {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .pill-btn.outline.on-dark {
    border-color: var(--blush);
    color: var(--blush-pale);
  }

  .pill-btn.outline.on-dark:hover {
    background: var(--blush-pale);
    color: var(--wine-dark);
  }

  .job-list {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .job-apply {
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .more-note {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
